id: pm-2jtbl8
title: "GH-824: core-field recovery must name dedicated flags instead of extension activation"
description: "Core fields passed through --field are misclassified as unknown extension fields, and close-validation warnings expose snake_case names without executable flag recovery."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: agent-ux,error-contract,github-intake
created_at: "2026-07-30T11:27:37.570Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-30T23:28:47.111Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-30T22:52:29.664Z"
completed_at: "2026-07-30T22:52:29.664Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Core field names passed to --field return the canonical dedicated update/close flag; close-validation warnings include executable flags; tests execute every rendered recovery command
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make core-field validation errors directly recoverable in one CLI turn
value: Agents can satisfy resolution metadata without guessing flags or activating irrelevant extensions
impact: Removes a deterministic dead-end from close validation and generic field setting
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: fixed
expected_result: Reserved core metadata supplied through --field names its dedicated CLI flag and close warnings expose executable flag recovery.
actual_result: "Core-field classification now returns core_item_field_requires_dedicated_flag before extension lookup, and close warnings render dedicated kebab-case flags."
